.Dd July 8, 2026
.Dt CELL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cell
.Nd manage a shared .cell bare repo and its jj checkouts
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm init
.Ar src
.Nm
.Cm new
.Ar name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
encodes a simple convention: a
.Pa .cell
directory holds one shared bare git repository,
.Pa default.git ,
and each cell is its own colocated
.Xr jj 1
checkout of it.
.Ss cell init
.Nm
.Cm init
bare-clones
.Ar src
into
.Pa .cell/default.git .
The result is a standalone bare repo, disconnected from the repo it
was seeded from.
.Nm
fails if
.Pa .cell/default.git
already exists.
.Ss cell new
.Nm
.Cm new
walks up from the current directory to the nearest ancestor that
holds a
.Pa .cell
directory, then clones
.Pa default.git
into a sibling colocated jj checkout at
.Ar name Ns .jj ,
wired to
.Pa default.git
as its
.Va origin .
.Nm
fails if no
.Pa .cell
directory is found, if the one found holds no
.Pa default.git ,
or if
.Ar name Ns .jj
already exists.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Nm
exits 64 on usage errors.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Seed a
.Pa .cell
in the current directory from an existing checkout, then start a
cell:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cell init path/to/default.jj/.git
cell new foo
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jj 1
